  <!--
    Glyph geometries, one key per meaning.

    Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons v3.50.0 (MIT), outline set,
    `icons/outline/<name>.svg`. Every feature glyph uses the 24x24 outline grid
    and names its upstream Tabler icon above the key, keeping stroke weight and
    optical balance uniform across sidebar, menus, toolbars, inputs and dialogs.

    Four keys are deliberately NOT from the library: Glyph.WindowMinimize,
    Glyph.WindowMaximize, Glyph.WindowRestore, and Glyph.WindowClose. They are OS
    window chrome drawn on a 0..10 coordinate grid so a 1.15px stroke lands
    cleanly on the pixel grid at every DPI inside 46x38 caption buttons.

    PathGeometry (not Geometry) because Geometry has no content property:
    its mini-language is what the Figures converter accepts.
  -->

